{
	chapter.20FA6DDE88A8F3AB.title: "Beyond the Nether"
	chapter.231570DE6A7FCD52.title: "When Dungeons Arise"
	chapter.6AC5E192FD50BBDD.title: "Into the Underworld"
	chapter.77EAA804883E19D8.title: "Welcome"
	chapter_group.0DB2701AC66EF66D.title: "Chapter 1: Introduction"
	chapter_group.39AF526352746E48.title: "Chapter 2"
	quest.00FE9CBEE0FC2521.quest_desc: [
		"&6&lThe Engineer's Workbench&r"
		""
		"Craft the workbench and a &bComponents Blueprint&r, then place the blueprint in the workbench."
		""
		"&eIron and Steel Mechanical Components&r must be made here. Their normal crafting recipes have been removed."
		""
		"You will need an &bIron Mechanical Component&r for the Dynamo and for the center of the Basic Engineering Block recipe."
		""
		"You will need the wire cutters to make the dynamo. "
	]
	quest.00FE9CBEE0FC2521.title: "The Engineer's Workbench"
	quest.0331AC0315EBB66D.quest_desc: ["Nestled among the trees, this lively tavern is usually a haven for villagers looking to unwind. Yet when the ale flows too freely, even the most peaceful patrons turn aggressive, defending their pub with surprising ferocity. Enter carefully or risk being caught in a drunken brawl."]
	quest.0331AC0315EBB66D.quest_subtitle: "Find a Greenwood Pub"
	quest.03340171A9F60D98.quest_desc: [
		"&6&lBefore You Go&r"
		""
		"Check JEI when a recipe is different from what you remember. Some recipes have been changed for this pack."
		""
		"[\"If you get stuck, read the other pages before assuming something is broken. If it still does not make sense, let me know in the \",{\"text\":\"Discord\",\"color\":\"blue\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"56FF4A052F4B1F4E\"}},\".\"]"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6&lFTB Essentials Commands&r"
		""
		"Before you head out, there are a few commands worth knowing. &e/sethome&r is a good place to start."
		""
		"Type commands into chat. Use &eTab&r to see the names and arguments available to you. Replace <name> or <player> with the name you want, without the brackets."
		""
		"Servers and ranks can change permissions, limits, and cooldowns. The values here are the current &epack defaults&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6&lSetting a Home&r"
		""
		"&e/sethome <name>&r saves your current location. For example, &e/sethome base&r."
		""
		"Use &e/sethome&r without a name to save your main home. Then just type &e/home&r to return there. "
		""
		"Save other locations with names, like &e/sethome factory&r."
		""
		"&e/home <name>&r takes you back there. &e/listhomes&r shows your saved homes, and &e/delhome <name>&r removes one."
		""
		"The default limit is &afive homes&r, with a &a5-second&r cooldown on &e/home&r. Set yours somewhere safe before exploring!"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6&lGetting Back&r"
		""
		"&e/back&r returns you to a previous location after teleporting or dying. "
		""
		"Super handy when you need to get back to your stuff."
		""
		"The default cooldown is &a5 seconds&r, and the command keeps up to &a10 locations&r in its history."
		""
		"Just...be careful if you died to a boss or something, as you are &c&l&oNOT&r&r&r invinicible while teleporting."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6&lSpawn and Exploring&r"
		""
		"&e/spawn&r takes you to the world spawn."
		""
		"&e/playerspawn&r takes you to your personal respawn point, such as your bed. Both have a &a10-second&r cooldown by default."
		""
		"&e/rtp&r teleports you to a random location in your current dimension, between &a1,500 and 5,000 blocks&r from its spawn reference. It has a &a60-second&r cooldown. The End, space orbits, void worlds, and pocket dimensions are excluded."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6&lTeleporting to Friends&r"
		""
		"&e/tpa <player>&r asks to teleport you to that player."
		""
		"&e/tpahere <player>&r asks that player to teleport to you."
		""
		"The recipient can use the &aAccept&r or &cDeny&r buttons in chat. The command equivalents are &e/tpaccept <id>&r and &e/tpdeny <id>&r; use the request ID shown by the command suggestions."
		""
		"Requests have a &a10-second&r cooldown by default."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6&lServer Warps&r"
		""
		"&e/listwarps&r shows the server's saved warp locations."
		""
		"&e/warp <name>&r teleports you to one. It has a &a10-second&r cooldown by default."
		""
		"Warps need to be created by an admin first. If the list is empty, there are no warps to use yet."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6&lA Few Other Commands&r"
		""
		"&e/near&r lists nearby players, sorted by distance."
		""
		"&e/leaderboard&r shows server statistics. Use Tab to see the available categories."
		""
		"&e/nickname <name>&r changes your displayed nickname."
		""
		"&e/recording&r and &e/streaming&r toggle announcements that you are recording or streaming."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6&lItems and Utilities&r"
		""
		"&e/hat&r lets you wear the item you are holding as a hat."
		""
		"&e/trashcan&r opens an inventory for throwing away unwanted items. &cItems put in it are deleted.&r"
		""
		"&e/kickme&r disconnects you from the server. It can help when you need to reconnect after getting stuck or desynced."
		""
		"&e/give_me_kit <name>&r claims a kit if the server has configured one and you have permission to use it."
		""
		"The next pages are for Admin Commands. If you are not a Server Admin, you do not need to know these commands."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6&lAdmin Commands: Player Tools&r"
		""
		"These commands require admin permission unless the server grants access through ranks. They are not ordinary progression tools."
		""
		"&e/heal&r restores health and clears harmful conditions. &e/feed&r fills your hunger, and &e/extinguish&r puts out fire."
		""
		"&e/fly&r toggles flight, &e/god&r toggles invincibility, and &e/speed <boost_percent>&r changes movement speed."
		""
		"Some commands also accept a player argument. Use Tab for the exact syntax."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6&lAdmin Commands: Inventories&r"
		""
		"&e/invsee <player>&r opens another player's inventory."
		""
		"&e/enderchest&r opens an Ender Chest remotely."
		""
		"&e/open crafting&r and &e/open anvil&r open those workstations remotely."
		""
		"&e/open smithing&r and &e/open stonecutter&r do the same for a Smithing Table and Stonecutter. These /open commands require admin permission by default."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6&lAdmin Commands: Teleporting&r"
		""
		"&e/jump&r teleports you to the block you are looking at."
		""
		"&e/teleport_last <player>&r takes you to a player's last recorded location."
		""
		"&e/tpx <dimension>&r teleports you to a dimension."
		""
		"&e/tp_offline&r, also available as &e/tpo&r, changes an offline player's location. Use Tab for its name, ID, and position arguments."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6&lAdmin Commands: Server Management&r"
		""
		"&e/setwarp <name>&r saves a warp at your location. &e/delwarp <name>&r removes it."
		""
		"&e/mute <player>&r and &e/unmute <player>&r control whether a player can chat."
		""
		"&e/kit&r manages the server's item kits. Use Tab to see its subcommands."
	]
	quest.03340171A9F60D98.title: "Before You Go"
	quest.041A1C64A8468087.quest_desc: ["Suspended high in the sky, this arrowhead-shaped airship drifts on a massive aft propeller. Boarding is perilous, but those who succeed will witness its strange and fearsome inhabitants riding boar-like beasts, their eyeless faces obscured by ominous cages. Danger and mystery ride with them across the clouds."]
	quest.041A1C64A8468087.quest_subtitle: "Find a Heavenly Rider"
	quest.05C509A67AF655B9.quest_desc: [
		"&6&lIt's Mining Time&r"
		""
		"You will need a few basic resources early in the game to get started, so I recommend you do the namesake of the game, &e&lMINE!&r"
		""
		"These resources will be used to get into &dArs Nouveau&r, which will introduce you to one of the major mods of the pack and also allow you to craft an &e&oEXTREMELY&r useful item, the Structure Compass."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6&lBefore You Head Underground&r"
		""
		"Gather the resources above, as that should cover what you'll need early in the game. It wouldn't hurt to grab more, though. You will definitely need to come back to the mines before Chapter 1 is over."
		""
		"Make sure to bring food and torches, and remember to set a home using &e/sethome&r. That makes it easy to get back to your base when you are done."
	]
	quest.05C509A67AF655B9.title: "It's Mining Time"
	quest.061098489E8FBE67.quest_desc: [
		"&6&lMaking Creosote Oil&r"
		""
		"Logs are an easy way to get &bCreosote Oil&r for your Treated Wood. A full batch of &eeight logs&r produces &eeight charcoal and one bucket of oil&r."
		""
		"You can also process &ecoal or Coal Blocks&r. Coal produces more oil and gives you &bCoal Coke&r, which you will need for steel."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6&lTreating the Wood&r"
		""
		"Put &eone empty bucket&r in the Coke Oven to collect the oil. Craft it with &eeight planks&r to make &eeight Treated Wood&r."
		""
		"Refill the same bucket and repeat until you have &e64 Treated Wood&r. You only need one bucket."
		""
		"Logs are fine for making oil, but &eCoal Coke is required in the Blast Furnace&r. You will need to mine coal before making steel."
	]
	quest.061098489E8FBE67.title: "Treated Wood"
	quest.079E519C570CF346.quest_desc: [
		"&6&lEasy Water Wheel&r"
		""
		"The pack ships with a &bwater_wheel&r schematic. Load it onto a &eBlank Schematic&r using the &bSchematic Table&r."
		""
		"This quest is optional. Not everyone likes building with oak and this schematic uses oak wood! "
		""
		"It helps bridge the gap if you have never used IE, since its Water Wheel works differently from Create's."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6&lPositioning the Schematic&r"
		""
		"Follow the schematic's on-screen controls to position it. The &efour oak-log pillars&r should sit at ground level, with the &ecobblestone base&r extending into the ground."
		""
		"Use this image to check the placement:"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/quest_pictures/water_wheel_schematic.png width:220 height:150 align:center fit:true click_action:none:}"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6&lGathering the Materials&r"
		""
		"Place a &bSchematicannon&r nearby with a &echest or barrel&r directly beside it. Put the positioned schematic in the cannon."
		""
		"Use the cannon's &bClipboard&r slot to print a material checklist. Gather the listed items and put them in the adjacent chest or barrel."
		""
		"Return the Clipboard to the checklist slot to refresh the list and check what is still missing."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6&lBuilding It&r"
		""
		"Put &eGunpowder&r in the Schematicannon's fuel slot, then press &ePlay&r. The cannon takes building materials from the adjacent storage."
		""
		"Once it finishes, remove the &ecobblestone&r and place the &ethree IE Water Wheels&r in a row starting on the lone oak plank at the back. "
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6&lAdding the Water&r"
		""
		"Go to the top and place &ethree water source blocks&r along the short edge with fences."
		""
		"That is the &eleft side when facing the Dynamo&r. The water should flow down over the wheels."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6&lConnecting the Power&r"
		""
		"Attach &eLV Wire Connectors&r to the Dynamo and LV Accumulator, then connect them with &eCopper Wire&r."
		""
		"Use your &bEngineer's Hammer&r on the accumulator face to set it to &binput (blue)&r for charging or &6output (orange)&r for powering machines. Put the connector on the configured face."
		""
		"It took me a while to learn this setup the first time, so hopefully this saves you some trouble!"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6&lThe Finished Setup&r"
		""
		"Here is the completed Water Wheel as an example of what yours could look like:"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/quest_pictures/water_wheel_finished.png width:220 height:150 align:center fit:true click_action:none:}"
	]
	quest.079E519C570CF346.title: "Easy Water Wheel"
	quest.0825CA29733DF21E.title: "The Blaze Burner"
	quest.0B89EB36AC565461.quest_desc: ["Deep within this subterranean city, the heat of molten lava and the hum of industry dominate the air. The Nether’s influence is strong here, fueling forges and animating Forge Sentinels that patrol every corridor. Only those prepared for fire and steel will survive, and claim the treasures forged within."]
	quest.0B89EB36AC565461.quest_subtitle: "Find a Foundry"
	quest.0CE50A7F4F1A0E4D.quest_desc: ["ladder stretches skyward, disappearing into the clouds. At its top floats a strange, floating vessel. What secrets or dangers await above, none can say… except that the view alone is enough to make even the bravest adventurer’s stomach turn."]
	quest.0CE50A7F4F1A0E4D.quest_subtitle: "Find a Small Blimp"
	quest.0E089FBA14DF8906.quest_desc: [
		"&6&lInto the Aether&r"
		""
		"Enter the Aether! It too is in this pack."
		""
		"Make &e16 Glowstone&r for the portal using the Enchanting Apparatus recipe in JEI (yes you could kill witches or something, but this will likely be easier at this stage)."
		""
		"Build the portal frame and activate it with &ea bucket of water&r. You'll need to come here a few times, so keep that portal nearby!"
	]
	quest.0E089FBA14DF8906.title: "Into the Aether"
	quest.0E80BD3DCDAB7372.quest_desc: [
		"&6&lChapter 1: Into the Underworld&r"
		""
		"The Nether is locked. To get in, you need to make and use the &dSeal of the Underworld&r."
		""
		"This chapter gets you started with Create and Ars Nouveau, then helps you make a &bStructure Compass&r. "
		""
		"You should also keep a &aBiome Compass&r handy too. You will be doing a fair bit of traveling."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6&lThe Four Pieces&r"
		""
		"The Seal Pieces come from the &eIDAS Dig Site&r, &eLich&r, &eAether Bronze Dungeon&r, and &eAlpha Yeti&r."
		""
		"You will need to build up your tech and magic between those trips. The &dSkybound&r and &dGrounded Sigils&r are part of unlocking the next Twilight Forest bosses."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6&lPutting It Together&r"
		""
		"You will also need to make the &dNether Crystal&r using Create, Ars Nouveau, and Mekanism, and capture &esix Nether Essences&r."
		""
		"Once it is ready, &e'eat' the Seal&r to unlock the Nether. Just having it in your inventory will not do it. "
		""
		"Everyone in your &bFTB Team&r must &ecraft and use their own Seal&r to unlock &cThe Nether&r. A finished Seal is bound to its crafter."
	]
	quest.0E80BD3DCDAB7372.quest_subtitle: "The Pre-Nether Expedition"
	quest.0E80BD3DCDAB7372.title: "Chapter 1"
	quest.102049B6088E4226.quest_desc: [
		"&e&lThis pack is in alpha!&r"
		""
		"I am still working on the recipes, progression, and quests, so expect things to change."
		""
		"If something is broken or confusing, tell me! A screenshot helps, and so does knowing how to make it happen again."
		""
		"&cBack up your world before updating your modpack.&r "
		""
		"Structure and loot changes may need fresh chunks or a new world (like normal, I assume you &e&oHAVE&r&r played Minecraft before)."
	]
	quest.131F6D9010B8AEF4.quest_desc: [
		"&6&lMaking Silica Compound&r"
		""
		"Mill &esand&r into &bPowdered Sand&r using a Create Millstone."
		""
		"Mix Powdered Sand with &eclay&r in a Basin above your filled Blaze Burner. Feed the burner fuel to heat the recipe."
		""
		"The resulting &bSilica Compound&r is used to make Blast Bricks."
	]
	quest.131F6D9010B8AEF4.title: "Silica Compound"
	quest.14857DBF1DCBF100.quest_desc: ["Cresting the waves like a shadow of the past, this cursed vessel is crewed by skeletons that seem impossible to keep down. Every deck hides danger, every hold whispers of lost treasure and every strike you land may be fleeting. Only the bold (or the foolhardy) dare to face its relentless undead crew."]
	quest.14857DBF1DCBF100.quest_subtitle: "Find an Undead Pirate Ship"
	quest.1635DD7388E05DC3.quest_desc: [
		"&6&lIntro to Create&r"
		""
		"This gets you into the basics of &6Create&r. With &efour Water Wheels&r and some small and large cogs, you can make a &e64 RPM&r network to power one Press, Mixer, and Millstone."
		""
		"This should cover your early game Create setup."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6&lIncreasing the Speed&r"
		""
		"Connect the four Water Wheels in a row and place a &bLarge Cogwheel&r on their shaft."
		""
		"Mesh a &bSmall Cogwheel&r with the teeth of the large cog. Going from a large cog to a small cog &edoubles the speed&r."
		""
		"Connect another large cog to the small cog's shaft, then mesh it with another small cog. "
		""
		"Repeat for &ethree large to small stages&r: &e8 > 16 > 32 > 64 RPM&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6&lKeeping It Compact&r"
		""
		"You can use &bAndesite Casing&r to cover cog shafts and prevent unwanted connections when arranging the gears close together."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6&lExample Setup&r"
		""
		"You can create something like this:"
		"{image:kubejs:textures/quest_pictures/early_create_setup.png width:240 height:135 align:center fit:true}"
	]
	quest.1635DD7388E05DC3.title: "Intro to Create"
	quest.188AAB5B74C6EAAE.quest_subtitle: "Discover an Infested Temple explorer map"
	quest.18FDF378F9BE60C2.quest_desc: [
		"&6&lGenerating Source&r"
		""
		"An easy way to generate the Source required for the Structure Compass is to use &aSnad&r and a &cRedstone Clock&r."
		""
		"There are two useful items that grow quickly on Snad when a redstone signal is pulsed on the block: &aSugar Cane and Cactus&r."
		""
		"Using an &aAgronomic Sourcelink&r, you can harness the growth for a quick and dirty early game Source farm. Put a Source Jar nearby to collect it."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6&lCollecting the Drops&r"
		""
		"Place a block beside the space where the next cactus segment will grow. It will break off on its own, so no breaker or pistons are needed. "
		""
		"Sugar Cane needs a separate harvesting setup, I recommend a piston on a fast redstone clock."
		""
		"Use a 1x1 drawer with a &eVoid Upgrade&r to store the drops and delete any overflow. "
		""
		"Use an &bItem Collector&r to automatically pull the dropped items into the drawer."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6&lOr Do It the Hard Way&r"
		""
		"Or you can sit there and manually punch Sugar Cane as it grows on the Snad like a madman until your Source Jar has &b2,000 Source&r."
		""
		"&oI did this in testing, do not feel ashamed.&r"
	]
	quest.18FDF378F9BE60C2.title: "Generating Source"
	quest.1C375606107C117F.quest_subtitle: "Find Keep Kayra"
	quest.1C8FFE53D06DE36F.title: "Nether Crystal"
	quest.1CCA31D9352C60E6.quest_desc: ["Clustered around a towering central “grandmother” mushroom, these villages appear quaint from afar. Yet the villagers within are far more aggressive than their old-world counterparts, hiding a cunning fierceness beneath their colorful caps. Approach with caution as this village may welcome the unwary only to spring its traps."]
	quest.1CCA31D9352C60E6.quest_subtitle: "Find a mushroom village"
	quest.1CE2D64C62594686.title: "The Metallurgic Infuser"
	quest.1CEF2A38948010A2.quest_desc: ["Out on the open seas, the &6Illagers&r have taken to the waves, commandeering massive galleys and swift corsairs. Their sails cast long shadows, and their cannons roar with fury. Only the bravest dare to board, for fortune favors those who seize it."]
	quest.1CEF2A38948010A2.quest_subtitle: "Find an Illager Corsair or an Illager Galley"
	quest.1DE26FBF8D6162F9.quest_desc: [
		"&6&lStarting Immersive Engineering&r"
		""
		"Gather &eclay and sandstone&r for your Coke Oven. You will use its &bCreosote Oil&r to make Treated Wood for your workbench and first power setup."
	]
	quest.1DE26FBF8D6162F9.title: "Starting Immersive Engineering"
	quest.1E311BE950695BFB.quest_desc: [
		"&6&lFTB Chunks&r"
		""
		"[\"Use \",{\"text\":\"FTB Chunks\",\"color\":\"aqua\"},\" to claim the chunks around your base. Your \",{\"text\":\"FTB Teams\",\"color\":\"yellow\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"61EA94ECBC1E5A96\"}},\" settings control who can place and destroy blocks, open chests, and use machines in your claims.\"]"
		""
		"[\"If you want to give someone access without sharing quest progress, make them an \",{\"text\":\"ally\",\"color\":\"green\"},\" and set their permissions in \",{\"text\":\"FTB Teams\",\"color\":\"yellow\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"61EA94ECBC1E5A96\"}},\".\"]"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6&lClaims and Chunk Loading&r"
		""
		"Claiming a chunk protects it from &enon-allied players&r, unless you have given them access in your team settings. Mob griefing is also disabled in claims by default."
		""
		"The chunk map shows how many chunks you can claim or keep loaded. The config settings can change those limits, but they are already pretty generous in my opinion."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6&lKeeping Your Base Running&r"
		""
		"Force-loaded chunks keep your base running while you are away, &eeven when your whole team is offline&r."
		""
		"The world or server must still be running. If it is not working on a server, ask the owner whether they changed the settings."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6&lClaiming and Force-Loading&r"
		""
		"To claim chunks, open the &bChunk Claim&r menu and &eleft-click and drag&r to select chunks."
		""
		"To force-load claimed chunks, use &eShift + left-click&r."
		""
		"Use &eright-click&r to unclaim chunks, or &eShift + right-click&r to stop force-loading them."
	]
	quest.1E7C5FC5EAF91CD2.quest_desc: [
		"&6&lYour First Power Generator!&r"
		""
		"Connect an &bIE Water Wheel&r to a &bKinetic Dynamo&r and place it in flowing water."
		""
		"Use &eLV Wire Connectors and Copper Wire&r to connect the Dynamo to your &bLV Accumulator&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6&lThe First Grid&r"
		""
		"Collecting the Dynamo, LV Accumulator, LV Connector, and Copper Wire completes your personal &eFirst Grid&r milestone. This unlocks crafting the &bMetallurgic Infuser&r."
		""
		"This quest exchanges &efour Copper Wire Coils&r for &efour Insulated Copper Wire Coils&r. You also get a &bthird Water Wheel&r for the setup below."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6&lAn Optional Schematic&r"
		""
		"[\"The pack includes a water-wheel schematic if you would like to use it. See \",{\"text\":\"Easy Water Wheel\",\"color\":\"yellow\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"079E519C570CF346\"}},\" for the schematic and setup guide.\"] "
		""
		"Do note that the Easy Water Wheel quest is available after you complete this quest."
		""
		"Build it yourself or use the schematic. Either way, you will have your first IE power setup producing 80 FE/t."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"Use wires and connectors as well as relays to move power. Remember to use the Engineer's Hammer to change your accumulator's face to input or output as needed. Also remember that it is Connector on accumulator to relay to connector on machine. "
	]
	quest.1E7C5FC5EAF91CD2.title: "Your First Power Generator!"
	quest.1F10BC33D22328BD.quest_desc: ["Time has claimed this once-sacred site, leaving its halls cracked and overgrown. Now, ghostly skeletons and trickster illusioners linger within, guarding little more than shadows of former glory. Though its dangers are real, the temple’s sturdy walls make it a tempting refuge for those seeking a foothold in this hostile world."]
	quest.1F10BC33D22328BD.quest_subtitle: "Find an Abandoned Temple"
	quest.2027538C9390B70E.quest_desc: [
		"&6&lFinding the Slider&r"
		""
		"To get started, you need to locate a &eBronze Dungeon&r."
		"[\"This is easy with a \",{\"text\":\"Structure Compass\",\"color\":\"yellow\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"4D707A738EB0F10D\"}},\".\"]"
		""
		"Inside, find and defeat the &cSlider&r and claim its &etwo Bronze Keys&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6&lUsing Both Keys&r"
		""
		"Use one key to open the dungeon reward chest and collect the &dSecond Mysterious Shard&r."
		""
		"Enchant the second key in the &bAether Altar&r to make your &bSkybound Key&r."
	]
	quest.2027538C9390B70E.title: "The Slider and Skybound Key"
	quest.21426F5EEC922866.quest_desc: ["Half-submerged in the oceans lie the petrified remains of a colossal beast, its skeletal form stretching farther than the eye can follow. Was it a creature of the deep, dragged ashore in ages past—or did it fall from the heavens themselves? No records remain, only questions carved into stone."]
	quest.21426F5EEC922866.quest_subtitle: "Find a Typhon"
	quest.241629BCC1A18BEF.title: "Nether Core"
	quest.2500D96A429C8278.title: "Seal of the Underworld"
	quest.29237400DEE5B1D9.title: "Using Osmium"
	quest.2A0A01BE836BB2AB.quest_desc: ["A monument of grandeur and mystery, the Shiraz Palace sprawls in every direction, its halls twisting and turning beyond comprehension. Its purpose remains unknown, but its size and opulence are undeniable. Travelers beware: without a companion, it’s all too easy to lose your way in this labyrinthine estate."]
	quest.2A0A01BE836BB2AB.quest_subtitle: "Find the Shiraz Palace"
	quest.2A1B0386B7987DD3.quest_desc: ["Vast and dreamlike, the Aviary stretches high into wtilight sky, its halls divided into four whimsical quadrants. Each one unfolds as a surreal scene—bright, strange, and perilous in its own way. To wander here feels like stepping beyond reality itself. Is this the journey’s end… or just another beginning?"]
	quest.2A1B0386B7987DD3.quest_subtitle: "Find an Aviary"
	quest.2B0B612E5826A3DA.title: "The Alpha Yeti"
	quest.2B70445E6CD99EDB.quest_desc: [
		"Strange structures have begun rising from the land. Mysterious dungeons, fortresses, and towers that pierce the skies. No one knows where they came from, only that they’re teeming with hostile creatures, forgotten treasures, and powerful secrets."
		""
		"Your task is to venture forth and uncover the mysteries of these ancient places. Each dungeon holds new dangers, but also the keys to survival: weapons, artifacts, and knowledge that will aid you in the trials ahead."
		""
		"Prepare yourself adventurer. &6Exploration&r and courage are the only ways to thrive in this world where the land itself rises against you."
	]
	quest.2C9C9917CB9926B2.title: "Powdered Obsidian"
	quest.2DB4F395EA26DF4B.quest_subtitle: "Find a Coliseum"
	quest.2EF1CC0CB01AF94D.quest_desc: [
		"&6&lCrafting on a Stick!&r"
		""
		"This is one of my all-time favorite mods. It lets you put vanilla workstations on a stick and access them with a keybind."
		""
		"The pack's default key is &eV&r for equipped workstation sticks."
		""
		"I suggest crafting the &bCrafting Table on a Stick&r first. The &bStonecutter on a Stick&r is pretty useful too."
	]
	quest.2EF1CC0CB01AF94D.title: "Crafting on a Stick!"
	quest.2EFC5DBD8122A0AE.quest_desc: ["Far below the surface lies a twisted network of chambers, where the air is thick with disease and shadow. Once a place of treatment, it now resembles a burial ground for forgotten rulers, its halls echoing with the whispers of those long lost. Only the brave (or the desperate) dare to tread these haunted corridors."]
	quest.2EFC5DBD8122A0AE.quest_subtitle: "Find a Plague Asylum"
	quest.3011E909FC1B3746.quest_desc: [
		"&6&lBrass and the Deployer&r"
		""
		"Make &bBrass&r by mixing &ecopper and zinc&r in a heated Basin. Use your filled Blaze Burner underneath it."
		""
		"Make Rose Quartz by mixing amethyst and redstone in a heated Basin."
		""
		"Use the brass to craft &bDeployers&r. You will also need &bElectron Tubes&r; check their recipes in JEI."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6&lMore Machines, More Power&r"
		""
		"To use the Deployers alongside your existing machines, you will need more stress capacity than your four small Water Wheels provide at &e64 RPM&r."
		""
		"Add more Water Wheels or slow down the network. I recommend upgrading to &bLarge Water Wheels&r and adjusting the gearing to keep &e64 RPM&r for now."
		""
		"Check your &bStressometer or Engineer's Goggles&r to make sure the network is not overstressed."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6&lGetting Into Early AE2&r"
		""
		"[\"You will need Deployers for the early AE2 recipes. See \",{\"text\":\"A Note on Sequenced Assembly\",\"color\":\"yellow\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"4EDFBF483367C110\"}},\" for how to run those recipes.\"]"
	]
	quest.3011E909FC1B3746.title: "Brass and the Deployer"
	quest.30C702C317C40A45.title: "Basic Control Circuits"
	quest.3137574A4EFAF2E2.title: "Imbuing Essences"
	quest.337B998BA11AABD0.title: "Refined Obsidian"
	quest.3A4E8891C21AE08C.title: "Improved Blast Furnace"
	quest.3C19F20F4ECF325C.quest_desc: [
		"&6&lBuilding the Coke Oven&r"
		""
		"Place &e27 Coke Bricks&r in a solid &e3 x 3 x 3&r cube. Right-click the center of a side with your &bEngineer's Hammer&r to form it."
		""
		"Logs produce &bcharcoal and Creosote Oil&r. Coal produces &bCoal Coke and Creosote Oil&r."
	]
	quest.3C19F20F4ECF325C.title: "Coke Oven"
	quest.3D1C0F80B74B27D5.quest_subtitle: "Arrive at a Lighthouse"
	quest.3E6717E36E2A5A2F.quest_desc: [
		"&6&lThe Imbuement Chamber&r"
		""
		"To craft an Imbuement Chamber, you will first need to find an &dArchwood Forest&r using your Biome Compass and cut down any of the colorful trees you find there."
		""
		"(If you happened to spawn in or near one, tough luck, you still need to make the compass. Trust me, it is useful later!)"
		""
		"Use that Archwood to craft an &bImbuement Chamber&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6&lYour First Source Gems&r"
		""
		"Check JEI for the Source Gem recipe and put the ingredient in the chamber."
		""
		"You do not need Source for this recipe, but it will take longer without it."
		""
		"Make a few gems. You will need them for a Sourcelink, Source Jars, and the Enchanting Apparatus."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6&lSource Gem Guide&r"
		""
		"You can find an easy guide to making Source Gems on my YouTube."
		""
		"{\"text\":\"Watch the Source Gem guide\",\"color\":\"blue\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"open_url\",\"value\":\"https://www.youtube.com/shorts/eyeqUv2ybuo\"}}"
	]
	quest.3E6717E36E2A5A2F.title: "Your First Source Gems"
	quest.3ECA226F08D5195F.quest_desc: ["Hidden among hills and valleys, the monastery stands as a quiet refuge in a world of rising danger. Here, villagers tend to simple lives of prayer and work, untouched by Illager conquest. Though the halls hold little in the way of treasure, their sturdy walls and peaceful company make this an ideal sanctuary for weary adventurers."]
	quest.3ECA226F08D5195F.quest_subtitle: "Find a Monastery"
	quest.3F2740A7A9AB2EE6.quest_desc: [
		"&6&lYour First Steel&r"
		""
		"Build a solid &e3 x 3 x 3&r cube of &e27 Blast Bricks&r. Use your Engineer's Hammer on the center of a side to form the Blast Furnace."
		""
		"Process &eiron ingots&r with &eCoal Coke&r to make steel. Mine coal and process it in your Coke Oven first. Charcoal no longer works in the Blast Furnace."
		""
		"Create's Mechanical Press turns &eone steel ingot&r into &bone Steel Plate&r. The pack's steel recipes have been sped up, so you will spend less time waiting."
	]
	quest.3F2740A7A9AB2EE6.title: "Making Steel"
	quest.410455182F69C1E5.quest_desc: [
		"&6&lThe Twilight Forest&r"
		""
		"Surround a &e2 x 2 pool of water&r with flowers, throw in a &bdiamond&r, and stand back."
		""
		"Then jump in when the portal lights up to travel to the Twilight Forest."
	]
	quest.410455182F69C1E5.title: "The Twilight Forest"
	quest.4118927D9D079DC8.quest_desc: ["Rising like jagged thorns from the ground, these massive towers are defended by skeletons entwined with deadly roses. Each level is heavily fortified, and flying rose guards patrol the skies above. Only those who ascend to the top will claim the treasures and secrets hidden within."]
	quest.4118927D9D079DC8.quest_subtitle: "Visit the Thornborn Towers"
	quest.436231715C11E3BA.quest_desc: ["Scattered across the wilds, small bands of Illagers set up camp beneath their distinctive purple tents. Though their supplies are meager and their loot scarce, their presence is a warning, the Illagers’ reach grows wider with every outpost."]
	quest.436231715C11E3BA.quest_subtitle: "Find an Illager Campsite"
	quest.44D115281B0BFB75.quest_desc: ["Whispers speak of a &9flying vessel&r that hovers above the world, shimmering with strange energy. Few dare approach, for those who return tell of eerie lights, warped corridors, and guardians not of this realm. Seek it out, if you dare—and uncover the secrets hidden within its metallic shell."]
	quest.44D115281B0BFB75.quest_subtitle: "Find a Giant Mushroom"
	quest.4743C99543F49D2F.quest_desc: [
		"&6&lThe Skybound Sigil&r"
		""
		"Use your &bSkybound Key&r in the Enchanting Apparatus recipe shown in JEI. Keep a &eNaga Scale&r for the center."
		""
		"Obtain &eNaga drops, a Bronze Key or Skybound Key, and your first steel&r before completing this ritual."
		""
		"[\"Need steel? See \",{\"text\":\"Making Steel\",\"color\":\"yellow\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"3F2740A7A9AB2EE6\"}},\".\"]"
		""
		"Crafting the Sigil unlocks your next challenge: &cthe Lich&r."
	]
	quest.4743C99543F49D2F.title: "Skybound Sigil"
	quest.4791FC0A2E834D85.quest_desc: ["Dark magics linger in the depths of these dungeons, woven into items, halls, and even the very air. Power awaits the bold, but so do twisted fates for the careless."]
	quest.4791FC0A2E834D85.quest_subtitle: "Find a Bathhouse"
	quest.4D707A738EB0F10D.quest_desc: [
		"&6&lThe Structure Compass&r"
		""
		"Using the magical properties of the Enchanting Apparatus, craft a &bStructure Compass&r."
		""
		"(It may be handy to keep &eBOTH a Structure AND Biome Compass&r on you. You will see why in just a bit!)"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6&lWhat You Need&r"
		""
		"&eCenter:&r 1 Biome Compass"
		"&ePedestals:&r 4 Source Gem Blocks and 4 Amethyst Blocks"
		"&eSource:&r 2,000"
		""
		"Put one block on each of the eight pedestals. The Biome Compass goes in the center and is used up in the recipe."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6&lFinding a Geode&r"
		""
		"To locate a geode, use &bFreecam&r and search underground. Then either remember where it is or set a marker using &bXaero's World Map&r. Right-click the map and choose &eSet Temporary Waypoint&r."
		""
		"The current default keys are &eF4&r for Freecam and &eM&r for the World Map. If you have changed them, check your controls."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6&lGo Get That Amethyst&r"
		""
		"Then go over and dig down."
		""
		"(I should not have to remind you to &c&lNOT dig straight down&r.)"
		""
	]
	quest.4D707A738EB0F10D.title: "Structure Compass"
	quest.4E0AB14C24416743.quest_desc: [
		"&6&lWelcome to Antarchy - Ascension&r"
		""
		"Antarchy - Ascension is a progression pack built around exploration, tech, and magic. You will need to get into different mods along the way, so do not get too comfortable with just one!"
		""
		"The quests in this book will help you get started and explain the recipes and unlocks that are different in this pack."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6&lThe Goal&r"
		""
		"Your end goal is the &d&lAscendent Keystone&r. This is &eTHE pack milestone&r, and making it will unlock &bcreative-tier items&r."
		""
		"Along the way, you will work toward other keystones, each with its own name and place in the progression."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6&lBefore You Start&r"
		""
		"Read the Welcome quests and check them off when you are done. Once you have finished them all, the final confirmation will appear and let you into &eChapter 1&r."
		""
		"There is a lot to do before the Ascendent Keystone. Get settled, try out different mods, and have fun!"
	]
	quest.4E0AB14C24416743.title: "Welcome to Antarchy - Ascension"
	quest.4E4052F7EAD4FDD6.quest_desc: ["Bright banners and painted walls lure travelers closer, but inside these towering strongholds, chaos reigns. Each floor brims with bandits and traps, their laughter echoing as waves of foes pour from endless spawners. Conquer the towers, and their riches—and notoriety—are yours."]
	quest.4E4052F7EAD4FDD6.quest_subtitle: "Find the Bandit Towers"
	quest.4EA4FB8A550E2A77.quest_desc: [
		"&6&lFTB Quests&r"
		""
		"Open a quest to see what you need and read its description."
		""
		"Some quests have more than one page. &eUse the page arrows&r or you will miss part of the instructions."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6&lRead the Next Page!&r"
		""
		"Congratulations, you read the previous page and clicked to the next page."
		""
		"&e&lREMEMBER TO DO THIS IF YOU SEE MORE THAN ONE PAGE!&r"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6&lDependencies and Dependents&r"
		""
		"The lines between quests show what needs to be finished first. Clicking into a quest and looking at the two arrows near Tasks and Rewards will show you its dependencies and dependents."
		""
		"&eDependencies&r are the quests you need to finish before starting this one."
		""
		"&eDependents&r are the quests that need this one completed before you can start them."
	]
	quest.4EDFBF483367C110.quest_desc: [
		"&6&lA Note on Sequenced Assembly&r"
		""
		"Sequenced assembly recipes can be done &emanually or automatically&r. Follow the steps in JEI in the order shown."
		""
		"The item becomes an &bunfinished component&r during the process. Keep using that same item until you finish all the required steps and repetitions."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6&lUsing Depots&r"
		""
		"Place the item on a &bDepot&r beneath the machine needed for the current step."
		""
		"For a &bDeployer&r, put the required ingredient in its hand. For a &bSpout&r, supply the required fluid. For a pressing step, use a powered &bMechanical Press&r above the Depot."
		""
		"After each step, move the unfinished item to the next machine. Repeat the steps in order until you have completed the number of cycles shown in &eJEI&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6&lUsing Belts&r"
		""
		"An easy way to automate a sequence is to place the required machines above a &bMechanical Belt&r. The item travels along the belt and is processed by each machine in order."
		""
		"Keep the Deployers supplied with ingredients. If the recipe needs multiple passes, return the unfinished item to the start until the sequence is complete by using a belt traveling in the opposite direction."
	]
	quest.4EDFBF483367C110.title: "A Note on Sequenced Assembly"
	quest.5052D842FA5BFDA0.title: "Osmium"
	quest.509E9CA83FBC780E.quest_subtitle: "Find a Fishing Hut"
	quest.5100CFAD43E7D67A.quest_desc: ["Rising like a monument to conquest, this sprawling fortress serves as a bastion of Illager power. Its many levels are patrolled by raiders and spellcasters, their banners declaring dominion over the land. Within its halls lie chambers of wealth, guarded by Evokers whose magic is as deadly as their stares."]
	quest.5100CFAD43E7D67A.quest_subtitle: "Find an Illager Fort"
	quest.52FECFF0BDDA7E9E.quest_desc: [
		"&6&lThe Second Mysterious Shard&r"
		""
		"Open the &eBronze Dungeon reward chest&r with one of the Slider's Bronze Keys to claim &dSeal Piece 2&r."
	]
	quest.52FECFF0BDDA7E9E.title: "The Second Mysterious Shard"
	quest.53AF2B722A69DCDC.quest_desc: ["Tucked away in the tall grass, this lonely house stands weathered and broken, its timbers groaning with age. Easy to overlook, it bears little more than the memory of those who once called it home. Still, even the smallest refuge can hold a story."]
	quest.53AF2B722A69DCDC.quest_subtitle: "Find a Small Prairie House"
	quest.541BBC35DA4F0B73.quest_desc: ["Sprouting from a cluster of towering fungi, this outpost of miners has carved their livelihood into the surface world. Ruthless and territorial, they will defend their claim with tooth and nail. Whether the giant mushrooms shield them from the sun or serve some darker purpose, none can say. One truth remains certain: the mine runs rich with ore, for those bold enough to claim it."]
	quest.541BBC35DA4F0B73.quest_subtitle: "Find a Mushroom Mine"
	quest.55B9FC2FDBCA17D5.quest_desc: ["If you haven't crafted one yet, now might be a good time!"]
	quest.56FF4A052F4B1F4E.quest_desc: [
		"&6&lThe CtrlAltDyleted Discord&r"
		""
		"Use the CtrlAltDyleted Discord to ask questions, talk about the pack, or show what you are building."
		""
		"If you are reporting a problem, include what happened and a screenshot if you can. I am often online and love to help people!"
		""
		"{\"text\":\"Join the CtrlAltDyleted Discord\",\"color\":\"blue\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"open_url\",\"value\":\"https://discord.gg/vfJQjDusZF\"},\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_text\",\"contents\":\"Click to open in your browser\"}}"
	]
	quest.580A2BACA71EC494.quest_desc: [
		"&6&lGitHub Issues&r"
		""
		"Found something broken? Report it through the pack's GitHub Issues page."
		""
		"Include your pack version, what happened, and the steps to make it happen again. If the game crashed, include the crash report."
		""
		"Check the existing issues first in case someone has already reported it."
		""
		"{\"text\":\"Open GitHub Issues\",\"color\":\"blue\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"open_url\",\"value\":\"https://github.com/CtrlAltDyleted/Antarchy-Ascension/issues\"},\"hoverEvent\":{\"action\":\"show_text\",\"contents\":\"Click to open in your browser\"}}"
	]
	quest.582C56657BA3A103.quest_desc: [
		"&6&lThank You for Reading&r"
		""
		"That is the Welcome section done. Check this off to reveal &eChapter 1&r."
		""
		"Have fun!"
	]
	quest.582C56657BA3A103.quest_subtitle: "Have Fun!"
	quest.582C56657BA3A103.title: "Thank You For Reading"
	quest.5C12F4CC1F6F6C32.quest_desc: ["Looming among the clouds, this massive airship bristles with defenses and hostile crew. Phantom-mounted fiends circle overhead, while fish-like raiders astride hoglins stalk the decks. Boarding it is no small feat. Tthose who triumph will etch their name among the few who dared challenge the skies."]
	quest.5C12F4CC1F6F6C32.quest_subtitle: "Find a Heavenly Challenger"
	quest.5DF4112EC13D86E3.quest_desc: [
		"&6&lGets the Job Done&r"
		""
		"The &bWrench and Engineer's Goggles&r are some of the most important Create items."
		""
		"The Wrench lets you rotate blocks and Create machines. Use &eShift + right-click&r to pick them up quickly."
		""
		"The Goggles let you see extra information about your machines, such as stress usage, speed, and more."
		""
		"They also have their own &eCurios slot&r, so consider putting them there."
	]
	quest.5DF4112EC13D86E3.title: "Gets the Job Done"
	quest.5DFD2FDAD41199CA.title: "Frozen Exanimate Essence"
	quest.5E61BA6960339FAB.title: "Bottling Nether Essence"
	quest.61EA94ECBC1E5A96.quest_desc: [
		"&6&lFTB Teams&r"
		""
		"Playing with friends? Use &bFTB Teams&r to make a team and invite them."
		""
		"Why play in a team? Well, your team shares quest progress, and team members can build and use things in your claimed chunks, depending on your permissions."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6&lPlaying at Your Own Pace&r"
		""
		"Don't want to share quest progress with someone, but want to let them interact with your villagers or use your machines? Consider making them an &aally&r!"
		""
		"You can always pick and choose what permissions to give to allies and non-team members. Check the &bFTB Chunks&r quest for more on claims."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6&lPersonal Unlocks&r"
		""
		"Your team shares quest progress."
		""
		"Crafting milestones can still be personal. Everyone must &ecraft and use their own Seal of the Underworld&r. A finished Seal is bound to its crafter."
	]
	quest.63116691C92FD576.quest_desc: ["A quiet spring hidden among the hills, its waters swirl mysteriously in the bottomless well. Travelers speak of subtle blessings for those brave enough to approach. Some even report a modest burst of speed for journeys ahead. Whether magic or rumor, the well offers a curious advantage to explorers."]
	quest.63116691C92FD576.quest_subtitle: "Find a Wishing Well"
	quest.638C732682F94DFA.quest_desc: [
		"&6&lThe Biome Compass&r"
		""
		"The Biome Compass is extremely useful for tracking down a particular biome that could be hard to find."
		""
		"It is also useful for locating useful biomes such as the &dArchwood Forest&r!"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6&lMaking Both Compasses&r"
		""
		"You will use a Biome Compass to make the Structure Compass, so it may be handy to make a second one to keep."
	]
	quest.638C732682F94DFA.title: "Biome Compass"
	quest.6447492FAA873F93.quest_desc: ["Suspended in the sky, this floating steampunk city glows in hues of orange and green. Strange, gear-driven inhabitants roam its platforms, each dominated by a singular central eye or monocle. Enter with caution, this mechanical hive is as clever as it is imposing, and its secrets are tightly guarded."]
	quest.6447492FAA873F93.quest_subtitle: "Find a Mechanical Nest"
	quest.64B315EA9471F315.quest_desc: [
		"&6&lHang Glider&r"
		""
		"Before you run off with your Structure Compass, consider making a &bHang Glider&r."
		""
		"Climb somewhere high and use &eright-click&r to glide, allowing you to cover large distances quickly."
		""
		"Pair it with a &eJetpack&r from &cCreate Stuff \\& Additions&r later to really boost your travel speed."
		""
		"Shoutout Link from BOTW ;) iykyk"
	]
	quest.64B315EA9471F315.title: "Hang Glider"
	quest.65E52CD92BA90C66.title: "The Mekanism Crusher"
	quest.66D894EAE0521E71.title: "The Third Mysterious Shard"
	quest.67030CEFEC1CEF37.quest_desc: ["Driven from their villages, these hardy merchants now wander the wilds, taking shelter beneath simple cyan and brown tents. Though weary from exile, they still offer trade and refuge to travelers brave enough to seek them out. In a world rising with danger, such camps are rare havens of trust."]
	quest.67030CEFEC1CEF37.quest_subtitle: "Find a Merchant Campsite"
	quest.6858E25E510AE0FA.quest_desc: ["Drifting through the skies like a colossal squid, this otherworldly airship bristles with defenses. Phantom-riding monstrosities circle its hull, while fish-like warriors astride hoglins guard its decks. To face the Conqueror is to battle a skyborne legion. And only the strongest will claim victory."]
	quest.6858E25E510AE0FA.quest_subtitle: "Find a Heavenly Conqueror"
	quest.68F204CE116B47ED.quest_desc: [
		"&6&lIt's Timber Time&r"
		""
		"Grab some logs and saplings to get started. The tasks accept &aany wood type&r, so use what you find nearby."
		""
		"Keep a few saplings for your base. You will want a steady supply of wood as you get into Create and Ars Nouveau."
	]
	quest.68F204CE116B47ED.title: "It's Timber Time"
	quest.69B409445F44B3AF.title: "The Lich"
	quest.6A0237FADC519965.quest_desc: ["From a distance, it looks peaceful. Fields of golden wheat swaying beside a proud windmill. But don’t be deceived: the Illagers tend no crops for trade. Behind the rustic facade lies a nest of evil, their blades as sharp as the sickles they carry."]
	quest.6A0237FADC519965.quest_subtitle: "Find an Illager Windmill"
	quest.6AEE8803174DD81B.title: "Grounded Sigil"
	quest.6B4C7A052034177C.title: "The Aether Freezer"
	quest.6BFE5D35265080E6.quest_desc: ["A sprawling underground stronghold, the Scorched Mines radiate in four cardinal directions from a central dome. Heat and shadows fill the tunnels, and danger lurks at every turn. Brave adventurers who navigate its branching paths may uncover riches, but only if they survive the hazards within."]
	quest.6BFE5D35265080E6.quest_subtitle: "Find the Scorched Mines"
	quest.6CB5ACBAAED66871.quest_desc: ["Shaped from the stem and cap of a giant fungus, this whimsical dwelling offers a rare touch of charm in a perilous world. Lightly guarded and easy to claim, the mushroom house makes for a delightful refuge, perfect for any adventurer who’s ever dreamed of calling a mushroom home."]
	quest.6CB5ACBAAED66871.quest_subtitle: "Find a Mushroom House"
	quest.6DB6E9074C07BE83.quest_desc: [
		"&6&lThe First Mysterious Shard&r"
		""
		"Similar to the Biome Compass quest, even if you stumble across a Dig Site on your own, you still need the &bStructure Compass&r. This is intended, so go make one. Be mad at me later :P"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6&lLooting the Dig Site&r"
		""
		"These Dig Sites dotted around the Overworld have uncovered ancient materials and stored them on-site."
		""
		"Retrieve the &dFirst Mysterious Shard&r and the &bfilled Blaze Burner&r. I wonder what you could do with those..."
	]
	quest.6DB6E9074C07BE83.title: "The First Mysterious Shard"
	quest.6E5F1866FA5658B5.quest_desc: [
		"&6&lThe Enchanting Apparatus&r"
		""
		"The Enchanting Apparatus will allow you to craft one of the most useful items in Antarchy - Ascension, the &bStructure Compass&r."
		""
		"Using it, you will be able to find structures without aimlessly wandering. There are a select few that I will hide to force you to use other methods. &o*cough* *cough* looking at you Cataclysm and AE2.&r"
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6&lSetting It Up&r"
		""
		"Go ahead and craft one now. You will need an &bArcane Core&r underneath it and &beight Arcane Pedestals&r for the Structure Compass recipe."
		""
		"[\"You will also need a Sourcelink and Source Jars. Any Sourcelink listed in the task counts. If you want a quick and dirty early game farm, check the \",{\"text\":\"Generating Source\",\"underlined\":true,\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"change_page\",\"value\":\"18FDF378F9BE60C2\"},\"color\":\"yellow\"},\"* quest.\"]"
		""
		"*Accessible after completing this quest."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6&lA Quick Tip&r"
		""
		"And thanks to Deimos, you are able to &eBLAST cobblestone and sand&r. Hope you found a Blast Furnace in a structure or something."
	]
	quest.6E5F1866FA5658B5.title: "The Enchanting Apparatus"
	quest.70327C3AC547B354.quest_desc: ["Marked by its dark prismarine and yellow terracotta roof, this temple has long since fallen to corruption. Inside, swarms of spider-like creatures creep through its halls, striking with venom and ferocity. To enter is to step into a nest where every shadow crawls."]
	quest.70327C3AC547B354.quest_subtitle: "Find an Infested Temple"
	quest.7052C9A5A804E866.quest_desc: ["A riot of color rises from the wilderness, marking the territory of a cunning band of raiders. Their homes are bright and inviting, but enter at your own risk. These defenders strike fast and often. Those who prevail will find spoils and secrets hidden among the lively façades."]
	quest.7052C9A5A804E866.quest_subtitle: "Find a Bandit Village"
	quest.730B249B3F5A4F0F.title: "The Fourth Mysterious Shard"
	quest.73D5EE5238C37982.quest_desc: ["In the wilds rests the skeletal form of a great creature. its skeleton stretching skyward like branches of pale bone. Whether a relic of forgotten myth or a beast once hunted to extinction, none can say. Its silent frame endures as a monument to creatures long lost."]
	quest.73D5EE5238C37982.quest_subtitle: "Find a Ceryneian Hind"
	quest.75A6591BBD45C461.title: "Nether Crystal Seed"
	quest.76A10455B5117CBA.quest_desc: [
		"&6&lAndesite for Create&r"
		""
		"Using your shiny new Biome Compass, track down the elusive &aAndesite Caves&r and harvest some Andesite. You will need it to get started with &6Create&r!"
		""
		"Bring back a stack. Andesite you find elsewhere counts too."
	]
	quest.76A10455B5117CBA.title: "Andesite for Create"
	quest.76DAECF378BA3F19.quest_desc: ["Far beneath the surface lies a labyrinth of rails and tunnels, carved by long-forgotten hands. The air is thick with dust and danger. Creatures lurk in the shadows, and the echoes of minecarts rattle through the dark. Yet for those who endure, veins of treasure and hidden chambers make the descent worthwhile."]
	quest.76DAECF378BA3F19.quest_subtitle: "Find a Mining System"
	quest.79D44307D1CD7C76.quest_desc: [
		"&6&lDefault Keybinds&r"
		""
		"Antarchy - Ascension ships with a default keybind set created by me, CtrlAltDyleted. It uses the vanilla keybinds for most vanilla actions, and many major mods like JEI and FTB Ultimine use their mod defaults."
		""
		"With that being said, I have made some changes to the keybinds for major mods like Morph, Hats, and FTB Quests to ensure that a wide range of modded actions are available without remapping."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6&lRebinding Keys&r"
		""
		"This does not mean that you will never have to rebind any keys. It just ensures that the core early game is playable right from the start. Once you get deeper into progression, expect to add more keybinds."
		""
		"The default keybinds were set using a &e100% keyboard&r, so some keys may be unavailable on smaller keyboards."
		""
		"This can be alleviated with two mods: &bKey Bundles&r and &bStudious Keybinds&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6&lKey Bundles&r"
		""
		"Key Bundles is available under"
		"&eOptions > Controls > Key Binds&r and allows you to set different bundles of commonly used mod keys, like opening your backpack and creating a new waypoint which both share the 'B' key by default."
		""
		"It lets you choose the action you wish to perform using a &bradial menu&r."
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"&6&lStudious Keybinds&r"
		""
		"Studious Keybinds takes it a step further and allows you to visually see what keybinds are set to which keys and which keys have conflicting keybinds. "
		""
		"It also has layouts for different keyboard sizes like 60% and 75%."
		""
		"To access it, go to"
		"&eOptions > Controls > Keyboard&r."
	]
	quest.7B649F6D17795B67.quest_desc: [
		"&6&lAfter the Naga&r"
		""
		"After defeating the Naga, return to the Overworld. The &cLich King&r will not challenge you yet, as you are not worthy."
		""
		"You've heard that the &cSlider&r has been boasting about how strong it is in the Aether. Maybe defeating it will give you the materials you need to show the Lich King just how worthy you are."
	]
	quest.7B649F6D17795B67.title: "The Naga"
	quest.7C74371387B1909D.quest_desc: [
		"&6&lThe Mechanical Mixer&r"
		""
		"Place your &bMechanical Mixer&r above a &bBasin&r and connect it to your Create network. It needs at least &e32 RPM&r to mix recipes."
		""
		"For heated recipes, place your filled &bBlaze Burner&r underneath the Basin and feed it fuel."
		""
		"The optional &eFilter&r lets you choose which recipe the Basin should make while the optional Chain Cogwheel is a handy tool you can use to link your Press and Mixer together in a row."
	]
	quest.7C74371387B1909D.title: "The Mechanical Mixer"
